1
00:00:04,129 --> 00:00:07,782
PIN-only login: no passwords, one PIN per business.

2
00:00:07,782 --> 00:00:11,000
A fictional demo business: Sunrise Sweets & Bakery, Pune. Mock data only.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,907
Your record is the source of truth. The agent compares every listing with it.

4
00:00:15,907 --> 00:00:19,001
Five mock listing sites. Look-alike businesses are never read or edited.

5
00:00:19,001 --> 00:00:21,865
The agent reads each site and compares meaning, not formatting.

6
00:00:21,865 --> 00:00:29,577
It reports what it found. Nothing has been changed yet.

7
00:00:29,577 --> 00:00:34,457
Every proposed fix is yours to approve or reject.

8
00:00:34,457 --> 00:00:39,000
NearbyNow belongs to someone else: zero edits, and a claim request is drafted for you.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,001
Approve, and only approved changes are sent. Then every page is reloaded to verify.

10
00:00:46,001 --> 00:00:55,002
Every step the agent took, who decided it, and what it found.

11
00:00:55,002 --> 00:00:58,661
ShopFront queues edits for a moderator. The agent waits and does not claim success.

12
00:00:58,661 --> 00:01:03,790
After approval, one click re-reads the page. VERIFIED only if it really changed.

13
00:01:03,790 --> 00:01:07,993
Per site and field: the original value, the intended value, and whether it is verified.

14
00:01:07,993 --> 00:01:12,743
Formatting-only differences are ignored. Export the table as CSV for evidence.

15
00:01:12,743 --> 00:01:16,647
Type it in plain words. Questions are answered from your record.

16
00:01:16,647 --> 00:01:23,799
Closures and edits get a preview first. Nothing is saved until you confirm.

17
00:01:23,799 --> 00:01:28,704
Upcoming festivals are flagged early, so closures are never forgotten.

18
00:01:28,704 --> 00:01:31,500
Who changed what and when, including what was verified on each site.

19
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:37,502
Test cases TC1 to TC8 run from one page, with input, expected and actual.

20
00:01:37,502 --> 00:01:45,025
A new owner finds their listings by score: phone, address and name.

21
00:01:45,025 --> 00:01:50,306
Matches are scored on phone, address and name. Nothing is linked until you say yes.

22
00:01:50,306 --> 00:01:54,002
The PIN is shown once. Only a keyed hash of it is stored.
